  "worked_solution": "The matrix represents a system of three linear equations in three variables, say, $x$, $y$, and $z.$ We obtain the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & 4x+y+2z=-3 \\\\  & y+3z=0 \\\\  & -z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third equation states that \n\n$$\n-z=1\\,\u27f9\\,z=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\ny+3(-1)=0\\,\u27f9\\,y=3.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute $z=-1$ and $y=3$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n4x+(3)+2(-1)=-3\\,\u27f9\\,x=\\frac{-3-3+2}{4}=-1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-1$, $y=3$, and $z=-1.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as \n$[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$",
